/span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">EPred</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> z}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/WP/Assertion.html#Std.WP.Assertion\">Assertion</a> <span class=\"fn\">Pred</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/WP/Assertion.html#Std.WP.Assertion\">Assertion</a> <span class=\"fn\">EPred</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/WP/Basic.html#Std.WP.WP\">WP</a> <span class=\"fn\">Prog</span> <span class=\"fn\">Value</span> <span class=\"fn\">Pred</span> <span class=\"fn\">EPred</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">R</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> t}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">op</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">R</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">Pred</span> → <span class=\"fn\">Pred</span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\">Prog</span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">F</span> : <span class=\"fn\">R</span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Prop</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`x` frames the resource `F` with respect to the operator `op : R → Pred → Pred`: `op F ·` commutes\ninto the postcondition of `wp x` for every postcondition.\n\nFor the meet `op = (· ⊓ ·)` with `R = Pred` and stateful `Pred`, this means running `x` preserves the\nstate identified by `F`. Other operators take a simpler resource, e.g. a cost counter `R = Nat`.\n","docLink":"./Std/WP/Frame.html#Std.WP.WP.Frames","kind":"structure","line":35,"name":"Std.WP.WP.Frames","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Std/WP/Frame.lean#L35-L45"}}],"imports":["Std.Internal.Order.FrameClosure","Std.WP.Basic","Std.WP.Conjunctive"],"instances":[],"name":"Std.WP.Frame"}